  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_032, a multimodal multiprofile model using scvi_n200, ResNet50, transformer aggregation, and concat fusion, with validation accuracy 0.6878 and F1 0.6585, clearly above the best RNA-only scvi_n200 transformer model at 0.6530. This suggests the current representation, profile setting, aggregation, and image modality are promising, but fusion strategy has not been isolated because only concat has been tested in the best configuration. config_033 changes only the fusion method from concat to weighted while keeping the rest of the best setup fixed, so it directly tests whether weighted fusion can improve performance or whether concat is already sufficient. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest evidence, avoids changing multiple factors at once, and reduces uncertainty about an important design choice under a limited budget."
}

